      "notes": "Scales 1, 0.73, 1.37 x 2.11, rotation 30 and the offsets (users 0-5, 7) are magnification or 1:1 and are reproduced to within 1 code (about 0.15 % of the values; the half-texel offset of user 7 about 1.6 %, all ties at exactly .5 that the GPU sends both ways). Fitted structure: a per-tap 4 x 4 least-squares kernel on the offset channel gives the four bilinear weights as exact multiples of 1/256; float bilinear weights miss by up to 341 codes, rounding fx and fy alone by up to 225, rounding each product weight separately (half even) by up to 457 (tie cases of fx fy = 128 mod 256), w11 rounded ties down: 1 code. Plain rounding of S / 256 leaves about 6000 values per map one code high at fractions 0.50-0.56; truncating v to 20 bits first (the n + 4 bit truncation of the AO and normal fits) leaves about 280. Float32 orderings of the sum (normalised taps, fma or pairwise) move the remaining count between 70 and 190 per map but none is exact; the integer form is kept for reproducibility on DX12 and Vulkan. Gap: minification (user 6, field A at scale 3.3, 3.3 texels per output texel) is not modelled. BilinearHQ there is a wider prefilter: away from the wrap seam the result is 16-19 codes below single-level bilinear (an effective shift of -0.069 texel toward lower bitmap indices in x and y) and the step response across the seam reaches 2 texels. Trilinear over a box-filtered mip chain (best LOD 1.3, with or without a shift) misses by about 3100-4800 codes; other mip chains (point, [1 3 3 1]) do not fit either."
