      "notes": "Scales 1, 0.73, 1.37 x 2.11, rotation 30 and the offsets (users 0-5, 7) are magnification or 1:1 and are reproduced to within 1 code (about 0.15 % of the values; the half-texel offset of user 7 about 1.6 %, all ties at exactly .5 that the GPU sends both ways). Fitted structure: a per-tap 4 x 4 least-squares kernel on the offset channel gives the four bilinear weights as exact multiples of 1/256; float bilinear weights miss by up to 341 codes, rounding fx and fy alone by up to 225, rounding each product weight separately (half even) by up to 457 (tie cases of fx fy = 128 mod 256), w11 rounded ties down: 1 code. Plain rounding of S / 256 leaves about 6000 values per map one code high at fractions 0.50-0.56; truncating v to 20 bits first (the n + 4 bit truncation of the AO and normal fits) leaves about 280. Float32 orderings of the sum (normalised taps, fma or pairwise) move the remaining count between 70 and 190 per map but none is exact; the integer form is kept for reproducibility on DX12 and Vulkan. Identical to BilinearHQ except under minification (user 6, scale 3.3): BilinearSharp is unshifted (within 3 codes of single-level bilinear away from the wrap seam) but its step response across the seam is wider than bilinear (non-zero about 1 texel from the seam). Trilinear over a box mip chain fits best at LOD about 0.39 (max 134 codes, float); not modelled, so user 6 keeps the bilinear residual."
