    {
      "entry_id": "resample-nearest",
      "subject": "UV projection with the Nearest filter, Repeat wrap",
      "status": "exact",
      "formula": "UV transform (all entries): output texel (i, j) of the 256 x 256 channel (row 0 on top) at u = (i + 0.5)/256, v = 1 - (j + 0.5)/256 (v up); (a, b) = (scale_u (u - 0.5), scale_v (v - 0.5)); u' = cos r a + sin r b + 0.5 - offset_u; v' = -sin r a + cos r b + 0.5 - offset_v (r = rotation, degrees; scale about the UV centre, then rotation about it; a positive offset moves the image towards +u/+v). Bitmap texel coordinates (row 0 on top, centres at integers): x = u' W - 0.5, y = (1 - v') H - 0.5, float64. Nearest: the texel (floor(x + 0.5) mod W, floor(y + 0.5) mod H), i.e. floor(u' W), floor((1 - v') H); its 16-bit code is stored unchanged.",
      "public_sources": [
        {
