      "notes": "Each of the 2 x 2 x 2 conventions (v up or down, rotation sign, offset sign) was tested on the eight maps: only v up, rotation by -r of the sample point and a subtracted offset reproduce all of them; the pattern texels are unique, so every output texel identifies its source texel. Scale-then-rotate and rotate-then-scale are equivalent on this corpus (no non-uniform scale with rotation). The field A half-texel offset puts u' exactly on texel boundaries, which floor resolves upward as fitted."
    },
    {
      "entry_id": "resample-bilinearhq-repeatnone",
      "subject": "UV projection with the BilinearHQ filter, RepeatNone wrap",
      "status": "calibrated",
      "formula": "UV transform (all entries): output texel (i, j) of the 256 x 256 channel (row 0 on top) at u = (i + 0.5)/256, v = 1 - (j + 0.5)/256 (v up); (a, b) = (scale_u (u - 0.5), scale_v (v - 0.5)); u' = cos r a + sin r b + 0.5 - offset_u; v' = -sin r a + cos r b + 0.5 - offset_v (r = rotation, degrees; scale about the UV centre, then rotation about it; a positive offset moves the image towards +u/+v). Bitmap texel coordinates (row 0 on top, centres at integers): x = u' W - 0.5, y = (1 - v') H - 0.5, float64. Bilinear on the stored 16-bit codes: X = floor(256 x + 0.5), Y = floor(256 y + 0.5) (8-bit sub-texel fixed point); x0 = X >> 8, fx = X & 255 (same for y); integer weights w11 = (fx fy + 127) >> 8 (round, ties down), w10 = fx - w11, w01 = fy - w11, w00 = 256 - fx - fy + w11; S = sum of weight * code over the four taps; the value v = S / (256 * 65535) is truncated to 20 fractional bits (V = floor(S 2^20 / (256 * 65535))) and stored as the 16-bit code floor((V * 65535 + 2^19 - 1) / 2^20) (nearest, ties down). No clamp needed. RepeatNone: tap indices clamped to [0, W - 1], [0, H - 1]; output texels whose u' or v' is outside [0, 1) keep the value below the fill (the stack base, 1.0, here).",
