      "notes": "Scales 1, 0.73, 1.37 x 2.11, rotation 30 and the offsets (users 0-5, 7) are magnification or 1:1 and are reproduced to within 1 code (about 0.15 % of the values; the half-texel offset of user 7 about 1.6 %, all ties at exactly .5 that the GPU sends both ways). Fitted structure: a per-tap 4 x 4 least-squares kernel on the offset channel gives the four bilinear weights as exact multiples of 1/256; float bilinear weights miss by up to 341 codes, rounding fx and fy alone by up to 225, rounding each product weight separately (half even) by up to 457 (tie cases of fx fy = 128 mod 256), w11 rounded ties down: 1 code. Plain rounding of S / 256 leaves about 6000 values per map one code high at fractions 0.50-0.56; truncating v to 20 bits first (the n + 4 bit truncation of the AO and normal fits) leaves about 280. Float32 orderings of the sum (normalised taps, fma or pairwise) move the remaining count between 70 and 190 per map but none is exact; the integer form is kept for reproducibility on DX12 and Vulkan. RepeatNone: inside the UV domain the taps clamp to the bitmap edge (wrapping instead misses by up to 38837 codes on the 1:1 pattern); outside it the fill leaves the channel below (here the empty stack, 1.0). u' = 0 is inside (user 7); whether u' = 1 is inside is not exercised. User 6 (scale 3.3) inherits the BilinearHQ minification gap."
